  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Software entrepreneur Edward Warrington moved from California to a farm near Austin, Minnesota, as a child. After graduation, he served four years in the Navy, then entered computer programming. He established his business in Minneapolis and expanded it with a second location in Birmingham, which became his home.\n\nWarrington also arranged for the business to continue if he could no longer run it. He placed his shares in a revocable trust that provided for a management committee to take over after his death or incapacity. A later trust retained his broad control while setting out provisions for his children.",
    "html": "<p>Software entrepreneur Edward Warrington moved from California to a farm near Austin, Minnesota, as a child. After graduation, he served four years in the Navy, then entered computer programming. He established his business in Minneapolis and expanded it with a second location in Birmingham, which became his home.</p>\r\n<p>Warrington also arranged for the business to continue if he could no longer run it. He placed his shares in a revocable trust that provided for a management committee to take over after his death or incapacity. A later trust retained his broad control while setting out provisions for his children.</p>\r\n",
